What Are Automotive Seat Motors?
Automotive seat motors are compact electromechanical actuators that power seat adjustments in modern vehicles. These precision components enable functions including:
•	Fore-aft positioning
•	Height adjustment
•	Backrest tilt control
•	Lumbar support mechanisms
Most operate on 12V or 48V systems, with advanced versions incorporating position sensors and integrated control modules for memory presets and automated adjustments. The transition to brushless DC motors represents a significant industry shift, offering quieter operation and extended lifespan compared to traditional brushed motors.
